    "body": "# GEM™ V3.0 — Final Brand-System Baseline\n\nGEM™ V3.0 is the owner-authorized final brand-system baseline under FA01, incorporating the defined-scope AR01, AX01 and HR01 corrections and RP01 promotion. Formal deferrals and artifact-specific external-issue restrictions remain in force; no evidence gate is closed by this release.\n\nThe approved attachments are the full Parts A–D PPTX files, all eight DOCX letterhead templates (English, Executive, Minimal, Arabic and bilingual), and the JSON/CSS token documentation. Part B is specification only; component implementation is not authorized. Part C remains WORKING EDITION / PENDING PRODUCTION VALIDATION. **Part D is a CONCEPT / NOT PRODUCTION ARTWORK portfolio**, with no manufacturing or supplier approval.\n\nThe Brand Owner separately instructed publication of the four Arabic/bilingual DOCX letterheads as direct attachments. Their CONTROLLED INTERNAL TEMPLATE / EXTERNAL ISSUE RESTRICTED PENDING D8 VALIDATION markings remain unchanged. Public distribution of these files is owner authorized; it does not establish completed D8 validation or unrestricted external-issue suitability. No PDF is included. D8 prohibits external PDF/DOCX extracts of Part A slides 37–39, 65, 66, 68, Part B slide 9, and Part D images with baked-in Arabic. Windows-native and PDF/D8 validation remain deferred/restricted where recorded.\n\nLegal/IP evidence is owner accepted under formal deferral and has not been independently verified in the repository workflow. Logo assets/vectors remain working assets with production-master acceptance pending; the kit is not attached. This release provides neither WCAG certification nor independent Legal/IP clearance.\n\nRelease commit: `4e8c7f18f73d9f4b368fcd735c1cd5e3725a879d`, on the controlled branch; `main` is not merged or changed.\n\nUse only the explicitly approved attachments as the release deliverables. Repository source archives contain historical and restricted controlled-source material and do not grant external-issue permission for it.\n\n## Known findings retained by owner instruction\n\n1. **B01 — Part B slide 2 retains stale current-edition wording:** “This edition is V3.0 RC2; it becomes APPROVED only by Brand Owner authorization (AC20).” The wording remains in the exact audited RP01 PPTX; the current baseline is V3.0 authorized under FA01 with formal deferrals. No corrective change is included. Evidence: `GEM_V3.0_RP01_Release_Artifact_Promotion/17_release_artifacts/02_digital_design_system/GEM_BRAND_DigitalDesignSystem_PartB_v3.0_20261009.pptx`, `ppt/slides/slide2.xml`; RP01 `04_RP01_Status_Label_Change_Register.csv` preserved the containing paragraph as a qualifier. The existing 112-assertion consistency suite passes but does not detect this contradiction.\n\n2. **B02 — automatic source archives contain restricted material:** the audited commit tracks four promoted Arabic/bilingual DOCX templates in `GEM_V3.0_RP01_Release_Artifact_Promotion/17_release_artifacts/05_letterheads/restricted_internal_only/`, together with historical PDFs elsewhere in the repository. GitHub automatically links ZIP/tar archives of the tagged repository, so excluding these files from uploaded release attachments does not exclude them from source-archive downloads. The repository was already public. The attachment allowlist does not imply that source archives are sanitized, and D8 external-issue restrictions remain documented. [GitHub source-archive documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/releasing-projects-on-github/about-releases).\n\nThe Brand Owner instructed that release proceed with both findings retained in memory and the release notes. This instruction does not establish technical remediation, independent validation, legal clearance or production approval.\n\nThe Brand Owner explicitly authorized publication of the automatic source archives with the restricted templates included. This is acceptance of the documented archive distribution, not completion of D8 validation or permission to treat restricted templates as unrestricted external-issue deliverables.\n\n### Owner-authorized letterhead attachment addition\n\nFollowing the initial release, the Brand Owner instructed “publish them” for the Arabic First Page, Arabic Continuation, Bilingual First Page and Bilingual Continuation letterheads. These four unchanged audited DOCX files are now direct release attachments, bringing the total to 14 files and all eight letterheads. Both B01/B02 findings and all technical validation limitations remain documented. No tag, release commit, main branch or file content changed.\n"
